Use case: precise-object-edit / product visualization. The reference is the exact red Pagani car, camera, lighting, and white studio for the FINAL FRAME of a controlled disassembly animation. Create an artistic EXPLODED VIEW of THIS EXACT CAR, preserving its rear-left elevated perspective, component orientation, materials and red/black carbon/red-blue livery. Do NOT make a different car, and do NOT close its already raised doors or rear clamshell. Preserve the same camera and floor: the carbon chassis stays centered at the original car's lower position and same apparent scale.
Separate into exactly EIGHT main groups with clear gaps:
1) the upper red/carbon body shell lifted upward, with BOTH doors still raised and engine-cover still in its raised pose as part of this upper body group, blue20 remaining on raised original door;
2) the existing rear wing detached upward/right;
3) the installed V12 engine lifted out of chassis, suspended to the right;
4) the exposed carbon chassis at original floor position, cockpit seats, suspension and brake discs visible, NO engine, NO exterior upper shell, NO tires left attached;
5,6,7,8) exactly FOUR detached complete gunmetal wheel-and-tire assemblies, all visible, two to the left and two to the right of chassis, separated from each other, hubs exposed.
All groups maintain their original matching perspective and realistic size relationships, not unrelated collage photos. Use the existing generous white space to spread parts, leave at least 8% clear edge margins around the whole arrangement. Ensure upper raised doors are entirely inside canvas. Surgical carbon and metallic detail, soft studio shadows, no text, numbered labels, leader lines or watermark. Same seamless white background, NOT transparent. 16:9 landscape commercial photographic visualization. Controlled assembly study, not debris or destruction.
